  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform electric field $\\vec{E}$ exists between the plates of a charged condenser. A charged particle enters the space between the plates and perpendicular to $\\vec{E}$. The path of the particle between the plates is a:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wqdfz",
      "text": "\nstraight line\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7AVaq",
      "text": "\nhyperbola\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Tw4fY",
      "text": "\nparabola\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "pvGIr",
      "text": "\ncircle",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "When charged particle enters perpendicularly in an electric field, it describes a parabolic path\n$$\n\\mathrm{y}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{QE}}{\\mathrm{m}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{x}}{4}\\right)^2\n$$\nThis is the equation of parabola.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/VqHMsArdHbgO4jc2PkWC0FcoDVX3L3D7RcxfYpW6qd8.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
